BT /F1 10 Tf 54 262 Td (including calibration gases, pressurised cylinders, lasers and rotating test rigs. Access is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 249 Td (controlled by badge and each area has a named area owner.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 227 Td (The Halcyon calibration lab in Leeds, Building C, holds certified test gases including hydrogen) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 214 Td (sulphide, carbon monoxide and methane mixtures used to calibrate and verify HX-200, HX-210 and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 201 Td (HX-220 detectors. Anyone entering the Halcyon calibration lab must first complete the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 188 Td (gas-safety induction GS-02, and must wear a bump-tested personal HX-210 monitor at all times) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 175 Td (while inside. Bump tests are carried out at the lab entrance station at the start of each visit) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 162 Td (and the result is logged automatically against your badge. If your monitor alarms, leave the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 149 Td (lab immediately by the nearest exit, close the door behind you and alert the area owner. The) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 136 Td (GS-02 induction must be refreshed every two years.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 114 Td (The Lumen flow rig in Rotterdam and the Tessera vibration test cells in Austin have their own) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 101 Td (inductions, which are arranged by the area owners. Laser safety training is required before) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 88 Td (operating any Lumen test bench with the cover removed.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54 65 Td (8.5 Display screen equipment and home working) Tj ET
endstream
